{"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK12DpopVerifierO","title":"DpopVerifier","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DpopVerifier"}],"symbolKind":"enum","roleHeading":"Enumeration","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DpopVerifier"}]},"topicSections":[{"title":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/Request"]},{"title":"Type Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/iatLeeway"]},{"title":"Type Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/accessTokenHash(_:)","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/canonicalHtu(_:)","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/thumbprintS256(_:)","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/verifyProof(_:request:jtiStore:)"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/dpopverifier"]}],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DpopVerifier","kind":"identifier"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The resource-server half of DPoP: given the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DPoP"},{"text":" header a caller presented, decide","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whether it proves possession for ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"this"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" request and ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"this"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" access token, and return","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the key thumbprint that ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AxiamRequestAuthenticator\/verifyTokenBinding(_:proofs:)"},{"text":" then","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"matches against the token’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cnf.jkt"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Why this lives in the SDK","anchor":"Why-this-lives-in-the-SDK"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"§21.7.2 is a ten-check list, and the contract is blunt about partial implementations:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"“Partial verification is worse than none, because it produces a guard that reports","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"success.”","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" Nine of the ten look optional until someone builds an attack out of the one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that was skipped, so they belong in one audited place rather than in every application"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"guarding an endpoint."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The two most often missing: ","type":"text"},{"code":"typ","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — without pinning it to ","type":"text"},{"code":"dpop+jwt","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", any ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"other","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" JWT","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"signed by the same key (an access token, an ID token) is replayable as a proof; and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"ath","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — without it, a proof captured on one request can be re-aimed at a different token","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"held by the same key.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The algorithm comes from the key, never from the header","anchor":"The-algorithm-comes-from-the-key-never-from-the-header"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"alg: none"},{"type":"text","text":" and RSA-public-key-as-HMAC-secret are the same bug wearing different clothes:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"the token told the verifier how to check the token","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":". This enum dispatches on the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"embedded key’s own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"kty"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"crv"},{"type":"text","text":", so an HMAC path is never reachable no matter what the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"header says."}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"DPoP proof verification — CONTRACT.md §21.7.2 (RFC 9449), contract 1.16.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/DpopVerifier/iatLeeway":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/iatLeeway","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"iatLeeway","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation12TimeIntervala","text":"TimeInterval"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"§21.7.2 check 7 — the ","type":"text"},{"code":"iat","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" acceptance window, applied in ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"both"}]},{"text":" directions.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/dpopverifier\/iatleeway","kind":"symbol","title":"iatLeeway"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/DpopVerifier/canonicalHtu(_:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Reduce a URI to its ","type":"text"},{"code":"htu","type":"codeVoi